      "message": "I think this is wrong.\n\nAt this point, borrow will either be d or -1\n\nIf it is -1, we need to add it, not subtract it.\n\nGiven input {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0}, the function as it stands outputs {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2, -1}\n\nIIUC, output should be {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, -1}\n\nIf you change 1178 to:\np256_sddigit borrow \u003d -(p256_sddigit)d;\n\n.. and L1181 to:\nborrow \u003d (p256_sddigit)P256_DIGIT(a, i) + borrow;\n\n.. then I think you\u0027ll get desired output, however at that point the function is basically the same as p256_add_d..\n\nSo perhaps you could just change p256_add_d to used a signed digit for the carry, and just pass a negative number to it for subtraction?",
